# Frontend Architecture (FSD Hybrid)

Source of truth: `docs/architecture/frontend.md`, `docs/architecture/design-system.md`.

## Apps & Shared Libs

- `apps/web` — tenant-facing
- `apps/admin` — back-office
- `packages/frontend/ui-kit` — presentation (`Button`; UI tech TBD)
- `packages/frontend/core` — RTK store, base API, auth/tenant/`can()`

Features live as **folders inside each app**. Promote to a `frontend-feature-*` lib only when both apps need them.

```
apps/web/src/
  app/        # providers, router, shell
  pages/      # routes compose features
  features/   # members, tenants, roles, …
  shared/     # app-local only (thin)
```

Import direction: `app → pages → features → shared` (+ workspace packages).

## Pages Compose Features

```typescript
// apps/web/src/pages/members/members-page.tsx
import { MemberList, InviteMemberForm } from '@/features/members'
import { useCan } from '@b2b-saas-starter-kit/frontend-core'

export function MembersPage() {
  const canInvite = useCan('tenant.members.invite')
  return (
    <>
      <h1>Members</h1>
      {canInvite && <InviteMemberForm />}
      <MemberList />
    </>
  )
}
```

## Feature Slice

```
features/members/
  api/members-api.ts
  components/
  hooks/
  index.ts          # explicit public API
```

```typescript
// features/members/components/member-card.tsx
import {Button} from '@b2b-saas-starter-kit/ui-kit'
import type {MembershipOutput} from '@b2b-saas-starter-kit/contracts'

export function MemberCard({member}: {member: MembershipOutput}) {
  return (
    <div>
      <span>{member.userId}</span>
      <Button disabled>{member.status}</Button>
    </div>
  )
}
```

## Shared Lib Boundaries

- `ui-kit`: presentation only — no RTK Query, no business rules
- `frontend-core`: state/data only — no presentational components
- Never import backend packages (`domain`, `application`, `infrastructure`)

## Forbidden

```typescript
// ❌ Feature importing another feature's internals
import { x } from '@/features/tenants/components/internal'

// ❌ Putting ui-kit components only in one app when both need them
// ❌ OpenAPI codegen as the internal type channel (use contracts)
```
